From adfba73fce964122706f12f8ef6674263f68b04c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 18:59:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip uninitialized vif link removal

Changing an interface from legacy to MLD and back can ask the driver to
remove default link 0 even though no matching link-add operation
initialized its BSS state.  The default mvif link object always exists,
but its WCID pointer is NULL in this state, and the removal path
dereferences it.

Return before deriving link state or touching the WCID when the link was
not initialized.  This only affects the unmatched link-removal transition;
links created through the normal add path retain the existing teardown
behavior.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/commit/c6b206f391358af2fee96389544162838505fd1f
Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/main.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -464,8 +464,13 @@ void mt7996_vif_link_remove(struct mt76_
 	struct mt7996_vif_link *link = container_of(mlink, struct mt7996_vif_link, mt76);
 	struct mt7996_vif *mvif = (struct mt7996_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct mt7996_sta_link *msta_link = &link->msta_link;
-	unsigned int link_id = msta_link->wcid.link_id;
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy = mphy->priv;
+	unsigned int link_id;
+
+	if (!mlink->wcid)
+		return;
+
+	link_id = msta_link->wcid.link_id;
 
 	/* Hw requires to destroy active links tearing down the interface, so
 	 * postpone it removing the interface.
